        "url": "http://localhost:3013/en/recipes/gluten-free-napoleon-cake?mode=ingredient&ingredient=schar-mix-b&amount=200&unit=g",
        "text": "Skip to content\nBake Again\n.\nRecipes\nSaved\nShopping list\nAbout\nEN\nRecipes\n\nCELEBRATION CAKE\n\nGluten-Free\nNapoleon Cake\n\nTwo cakes with six thin 28 cm layers each, warm custard and nuts.\n\nCalculated\n\nQuantities scaled. This version has not been bake-tested.\n\nACTIVE TIME\n1 hour\nYIELD\n0.89 cakes\nDIFFICULTY\nAdvanced\n\nBest served the next day.\n\nFLOUR\nSchär Mix B + tapioca and corn starch\nJump to ingredients\nJump to steps\n\nBEFORE YOU START\n\nPlan for the rest.\nKeep this in mind\n\nHave enough sheets of baking parchment for 12 layers: each is rolled between two sheets and baked on the lower one.\n\nKeep this in mind\n\nPlan a day ahead: the dough discs chill for at least 2 hours, and the assembled cake rests for 1 hour at room temperature and 12–24 hours in the refrigerator.\n\nCALCULATED CONFIGURATION\n\nAdjust recipe\n\nScale the recorded base or calculate quantities from a supported ingredient you have. A form or pan size appears only when the source defines it.\n\nScale recipe\nUse what I have\nAVAILABLE SCHÄR MIX B BREAD FLOUR MIX\ng\n\nCalculated: 0.44× the recorded base. Check eggs and other whole items manually when the result is fractional.\n\nIngredients\nTo shopping list…\nLayers\nSchär Mix B Bread flour mix\n200 g\n10 tbsp\ntapioca starch\n35.56 g\n2.37 tbsp\ncorn starch\n17.78 g\n2.54 tbsp\nxanthan gum\nonly if the flour mix does not contain it\n1.33 g\n0.44 tsp\nbaking powder\n3.56 g\n0.71 tsp\nsalt\n1.5 g\n0.25 tsp\nsugar\n8.89 g\n0.44 tbsp\nbutter\ncold, cut into cubes\n53.33 g\nsunflower oil\n22.22 g\nsour cream\n111.11 g\neggs\n0.89 pcs\nlemon juice\n0.44 tbsp\ncold water\nas needed\n13.33–31.11 ml\nCustard\nmilk\n1,111.11 ml\neggs\n1.78 pcs\nsugar\n177.78 g\n8.89 tbsp\ncorn starch\n75.56 g\n10.79 tbsp\ntapioca starch\n8.89 g\n0.59 tbsp\nbutter\n44.44 g\nvanilla sugar\n10.67 g\nsalt\n1 pinch\nNuts and finish\nwalnuts\n66.67 g\nflaked almonds\n22.22 g\n\nMETHOD · 19 STEPS\n\nMake it step by step.\nCook step by step\n\nOne step at a time, with ingredients and timers close at hand.\n\n5–10 SEC\n\n01\nMix the dry ingredients\n\nIn a food processor, mix the Schär Mix B, both starches, xanthan, baking powder, salt and sugar for 5–10 seconds.\n\n10–15 MIN\n\n02\nCut in the cold butter\n\nCube the cold butter, freeze it for 10–15 minutes, add it to the dry mixture and pulse about ten times.\n\nCHECKPOINTThe crumb should be uneven: some sandy, with some pea-sized pieces of butter.\n\n1\n2\n3\n03\nMix the wet ingredients\n\nMix the eggs, chosen cultured dairy, sunflower oil and lemon juice only until smooth.\n\n04\nBring the dough together\n\nPour the liquid into the dry mixture and combine with short pulses. Add cold water as needed.\n\nCHECKPOINTThe dough should gather into clumps, feel pliable and not become a sticky paste.\n\n1\n2\n05\nFold the dough\n\nQuickly bring the dough together by hand, fold it 2–3 times and shape it into a disc. Do not knead for long.\n\nAT LEAST 2 HOURS\n\n06\nDivide and chill\n\nDivide the dough into 5.33 discs, wrap each one and chill for at least 2 hours; they may be left overnight.\n\n5–10 MIN\n\n07\nSoften one disc\n\nTake out one disc at a time. If it is very firm, leave it on the counter for 5–10 minutes.\n\n08\nRoll and trim a layer\n\nTIPRoll the layer on the parchment used for baking so the thin dough does not need to be transferred.\n\nRoll the disc between two sheets of parchment to about 1.5 mm thick. Cut a 28 cm circle, leave the scraps beside it and prick with a fork.\n\n7–10 MIN · 190°C\n\n09\nBake the layer\n\nBake the layer with its scraps at 190°C for about 7–10 minutes.\n\nCHECKPOINTThe layer should be light golden.\n\n10\nHeat the milk\n\nSet aside 266.67–288.89 ml of cold milk. Heat the remaining milk until almost boiling.\n\n11\nMix the custard base\n\nIn a large bowl, combine the sugar, both starches, vanilla sugar and salt. Add the reserved cold milk and stir until smooth, then add the four eggs.\n\n12\nTemper the egg mixture\n\nWhisk 2–3 ladlefuls of hot milk into the egg and starch mixture, then return everything to the saucepan.\n\n30–60 SEC\n\n13\nCook the custard\n\nCook over medium heat, whisking constantly. After the first bubbles appear, cook for another 30–60 seconds.\n\nCHECKPOINTStart the final 30–60 seconds when the first bubbles appear.\n\n14\nAdd the butter\n\nRemove the custard from the heat, add the butter and stir until smooth.\n\n8–10 MIN · 160°C\n\n15\nToast the walnuts\n\nToast the walnuts at 160°C for 8–10 minutes.\n\n4–5 MIN · 160°C\n\n16\nToast the almonds\n\nToast the flaked almonds at 160°C for 4–5 minutes.\n\n17\nAssemble the cakes\n\nAssemble two cakes with six layers each. Use the custard while warm. Spread it on every layer, adding walnuts to every other layer. Finish with layer crumbs and flaked almonds.\n\n1 HOUR\n\n18\nRest at room temperature\n\nAfter assembly, leave the cake at room temperature for about 1 hour.\n\n12–24 HOURS\n\n19\nChill overnight\n\nRefrigerate the cake for 12–24 hours. It tastes best the next day.\n\nBake Again\n.\nAbout\nPrivacy and your saved items",
